From 707a23bf903f1822d7070be2698ae758517c9110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:18:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [dialogs] Player information: Input, Processing and Output
 columns

Player information listed Kodi's player fields, so nothing showed what
a Dolby Vision or HDR file carries, what the engine does with it, or
what goes to the display. Redesign it, after the layout of the
libreelec-x86-DV build's panel (CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV#92), in three
columns: Input (the stream, its colour, its Dolby Vision configuration
and RPU levels), Processing (the engine's reconstruction, chroma
mapping, filters and GPU time, the static, RPU and HDR10+ metadata) and
Output (the mode, the signal, the tunnel and its infoframe), with
meters for the engine, CPU, memory, cache, drops and temperature.

While the dialog is shown, the DRM PRIME renderer describes the picture
on screen twice a second (CDataCacheCore::SetVideoPlayerInfo) and the
dialog sets those as window properties. The engine profiles each render
(three GPU timestamps) for its GPU time.

Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
